    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThis behavior is [more or less documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b21cd5b1b330844e4c4b93d65e99ecb7c79a63c9/doc/mini-cursorword.txt#L53-L55) and I don't think exporting the variation on `highlight()` is worth it (and having to also export `unhighlight()` is one of the top reasons).\n\nTo immediately update highlighting, manually triggering the `CursorMoved` event looks like a reasonable solution here. So something like this:\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>cw', function() vim.g.minicursorword_disable = not vim.g.minicursorword_disable; vim.cmd('doautocmd CursorMoved') end)\n```\n\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2025-03-14T10:32:00Z",
